Vendored subset of Boost 1.89.0
===============================

Why this exists
---------------

compiler/include/aros/preprocessor/ includes Boost unconditionally, and
inline/posixc.h reaches it, so any C source that touches proto/posixc.h needs
Boost headers present in the SDK. Nine AROS SDK headers use 23 distinct
BOOST_PP_* macros, including BOOST_PP_REPEAT, BOOST_PP_EQUAL, BOOST_PP_DIV,
BOOST_PP_MUL, BOOST_PP_ARRAY_* and BOOST_PP_TUPLE_ENUM.

The relocatable toolchain producer builds offline from a verified source set,
and ports-includes is deliberately outside its dependency closure, so the
fetched Boost Port in ../mmakefile.src is unavailable there. Without these
headers the produced package ships a Developer/include whose own headers do
not compile.

The full 1.89.0 source archive is 190099283 bytes for what amounts to two
header directories, which is why the subset is carried here instead.

Provenance
----------

Two of Boost's own modular libraries, at the 1.89.0 release tag, unmodified:

  boost/preprocessor, boost/preprocessor.hpp
      https://github.com/boostorg/preprocessor  tag boost-1.89.0
      archive sha256 53de1b2e64706b73903d9f3957525fa8fa620445ec0d596aa6fb8335af6f45c0
      taken from include/boost/ in that archive

  boost/config, boost/config.hpp, boost/cstdint.hpp,
  boost/cxx11_char_types.hpp, boost/limits.hpp, boost/version.hpp,
  boost/detail
      https://github.com/boostorg/config  tag boost-1.89.0
      archive sha256 a16a53f8f0dde2a9ff485fb134a069e54aca738009d825837dac9a35cd4afe0a
      taken from include/boost/ in that archive

The checksums record what was taken. They are not a build-time pin: GitHub
generates those archives on demand and does not guarantee their bytes over
time, which is one reason the headers are carried here rather than fetched.

Both libraries are kept whole. 301 of the 498 files are reachable from the
AROS SDK headers today; pruning to those would need redoing whenever an AROS
header starts using another macro.

Updating
--------

Replace boost/preprocessor and boost/config from the same tag of both
repositories, keep the version in ../mmakefile.src (BOOSTVERSION) in step, and
re-run the closure check: every boost/... include reachable from
compiler/include/aros/ must resolve inside this directory.

